{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1272745-interrupted-rhapsody","id":1272745,"title":"Interrupted Rhapsody","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-12-03T19:03:08-08:00","id":1272745,"title":"Interrupted Rhapsody","content":"What do you think would happen if a rhapsody were interrupted and the glamour soaked creation were never destroyed? Would the artist have a normal life? Would they still be able to create? What would other fae think of the creation? Chewing on this for a scene in Mage. I &lt;3 Crossovers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-03T19:49:37-08:00","id":1272759,"title":"","content":"I'd Treat the artist as Ravaged but still able to heal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-04T03:00:26-08:00","id":1272808,"title":"","content":"Especially when using Mage, the result is depending very much on the actions the PCs take. There are multiple options Mages have to interrupt Rhapsody. A technique my friends PC used on this was an extended spell, channeling the Glamour (aka Quintessence with a kind of dream resonance) from the dreamer, thus freeing it and dispersing it in the surrounding, so the &quot;dreaming Quintessence resonance cascade&quot;, that would be called Rhapsody by the Kithain, could not become worse.<br /> The dreamer in question was already in the act of creating, thus he was damaged by the process. My ruling was that in this case, he would be in a state similar to a heavy (or repeated) ravaging. A serious condition, but nothing that would be necessarily permanent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13221-thevarulfen","name":"TheVarulfen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"179"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-04T14:17:43-08:00","id":1272886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheVarulfen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1272745-interrupted-rhapsody?p=1272808#post1272808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Especially when using Mage, the result is depending very much on the actions the PCs take. There are multiple options Mages have to interrupt Rhapsody. A technique my friends PC used on this was an extended spell, channeling the Glamour (aka Quintessence with a kind of dream resonance) from the dreamer, thus freeing it and dispersing it in the surrounding, so the &quot;dreaming Quintessence resonance cascade&quot;, that would be called Rhapsody by the Kithain, could not become worse.<br /> The dreamer in question was already in the act of creating, thus he was damaged by the process. My ruling was that in this case, he would be in a state similar to a heavy (or repeated) ravaging. A serious condition, but nothing that would be necessarily permanent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-07T12:25:48-08:00","id":1273296,"title":"","content":"I would say that preventing the artwork from being destroyed is irrelevant. The point of rhapsody is that the artist pushes themselves beyond their limits in order to create. You'd have to prevent the artwork from being finished to protect them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-09T00:52:18-08:00","id":1273561,"title":"","content":"I'd rule that it would create a sort of living-anchor that the artist was dependant on. They would probably become massively famous from it, but be one of those 'quirky' art types that is only able to get away with their madness because of their fame.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile the artwork itself would become like a Glade Stone, radiating Glamour and probably attracting all sorts of twisted chimera. Changelings would be drawn to it, many of which would be seeking to devour it.<br /> <br /> If the artist in question is a Mage then...well this sound like a dangerous step towards becoming a Marauder...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3959-urabyfirst","name":"Urabyfirst","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}